{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1777134912,"nonce":"xNKTP9sSpeeCZc6i1Y3t6QS6aM8=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABAgIqNQ","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/88","origin":"github"},"title":"BizzyBoat dynamics calibration — focused on-water field experiment","message":"## Motivation\n\nPreliminary boat-dynamics analysis from the 2026-04-24 in-water bag (see [`docs/bizzyboat_dynamics_2026-04-24.md`](../blob/jazzy/docs/bizzyboat_dynamics_2026-04-24.md) once landed) shows the **PWM → speed → V-drop** curve has informative coverage at idle, 1.4 kt, and 3.4 kt, but is sparse where it matters most for cruise selection (PWM 1750–1900). Also the curve has a non-monotonic step around PWM 1640–1660 that's currently a \"looks like a planing transition\" guess based on small-bin samples — needs more data to characterize.\n\nA focused calibration run would give us a clean characterization that drives operational defaults (cruise PWM, expected energy-per-meter at survey speeds, reasonable acceleration assumptions for autonomy).\n\n**Scope note**: this is **not** in scope for the June 2026 class — students aren't doing this. It's for me when I have time.\n\n## Procedure (proposed)\n\nBench-power-on at the dock, deploy by crane as usual, and run a structured PWM sweep with reciprocal-pair cancellation:\n\n1. **Zero baseline** — at neutral PWM 1500, 60 s to capture idle voltage drift.\n2. **Sweep** — for each target PWM in `{1550, 1600, 1650, 1700, 1750, 1800, 1850, 1900, 1950}`:\n   - Hold for 60 s in MANUAL mode (operator commits one PWM, doesn't move the stick)\n   - Run **reciprocal pairs** at each PWM: 60 s heading approximately `θ`, then 60 s heading approximately `θ + 180°`. Averaging across the pair cancels current/wind contribution to body-x speed, isolating the PWM→thrust calibration from environmental drift.\n   - Pick `θ` to align with prevailing harbor current at the time (avoids fighting current at high PWM).\n3. **Acceleration step** — from idle, step PWM directly to 1700 / 1800 / 1900 and measure time-to-settle. Three reps each.\n4. **Repeat** at high battery state (start of session) and lower state (end of session) to characterize voltage-droop dependence.\n\nTotal water time: ~25 minutes for the sweep + 5 min for acceleration steps. Well inside one 30-min weather window.\n\n## Outputs (deliverables)\n\n- Updated [`bizzyboat_dynamics_2026-04-24.md`](../blob/jazzy/docs/bizzyboat_dynamics_2026-04-24.md) (or a follow-on dated doc) with:\n  - Filled-in PWM → speed curve (no gaps in 1700–1900)\n  - V-drop vs. PWM with proper baseline (battery-state corrected)\n  - Reciprocal-pair-averaged calibration values (no current bias)\n  - Acceleration capability table (PWM step → settle time)\n  - **Recommended cruise PWM defaults** for 1.5 kt / 2 kt / 3 kt with confidence intervals\n- Optional: a small Python helper (script or rqt plugin) that consumes a bag and recomputes the curve after each future field session — so the calibration is rerun-able as the boat ages.\n\n## Stretch — power, not just V-drop\n\nThe Cube doesn't read battery current today (per `project_bizzyboat_autonomy_stack.md` memory: \"no analog/CAN output to the Cube\"). If we ever wire a current sensor (e.g., on the throttle leg of each Torqeedo, or a hall-effect clamp on the main pack lead), the same procedure produces a real **power-vs-speed drag curve** and **energy-per-meter** numbers, not the V-drop proxy. That's a separate hardware task, but worth keeping linked.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- PWM-speed curve has ≥30 valid steady-state samples in every 50-μs bin from 1500 to 1950\n- Reciprocal-pair averaging applied; results documented\n- Recommended cruise defaults committed to `bizzyboat.yaml` (or wherever speed setpoints live) with the calibration date stamped\n- Doc cross-referenced from `MEMORY.md` so future agents can find it\n\n## Related\n\n- [`docs/bizzyboat_dynamics_2026-04-24.md`](../blob/jazzy/docs/bizzyboat_dynamics_2026-04-24.md) — the preliminary findings this builds on (to be merged separately)\n- `project_bizzyboat_autonomy_stack.md` memory — current sensor not wired, blocking real power numbers\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)`","files":null}]}